# Frontend (Vite) environment variables. Copy to `.env.local` (git-ignored)
# to override locally — never commit a real `.env.local`.
#
# Default (this var unset): the app runs fully local — in-memory data,
# bootstrapped from/backed up to IndexedDB, no network calls to any API.
# This is the mode every build ships with unless explicitly overridden.
#
# VITE_API_BASE_URL — opt-in "remote mode". When set, the app talks to a
# real GOMS backend (apps/api) instead of local IndexedDB: the tRPC client
# points at `${VITE_API_BASE_URL}/api/trpc`, local IndexedDB bootstrap is
# skipped entirely (src/main.tsx), and the server's own database backups
# apply instead of local IndexedDB ones. Never set by default in any build
# config — set it only to point at a specific deployed backend for local
# testing.
#
#   Dev backend example:  VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://goms-api-<hash>-<region>.a.run.app
#   Prod (hosted build):  VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://goms-prod.web.app
#                         — same origin as the site itself; Firebase Hosting's
#                         /api/** rewrite forwards to Cloud Run (firebase.json).
#
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=

# VITE_API_ENV_LABEL — optional. Overrides the environment name shown in the
# top bar's "Connected to …" badge. Only needed when VITE_API_BASE_URL's host
# does not carry the project name: a Firebase Hosting origin
# (`goms-prod.web.app`) is resolved automatically, a direct Cloud Run host
# (`goms-api-<hash>-<region>.a.run.app`) is not and falls back to showing the
# host itself. See src/lib/api-environment.ts.
#
#   Dev backend example:  VITE_API_ENV_LABEL=goms-dev
#
# VITE_API_ENV_LABEL=

# VITE_BID_TRACKER_ENABLED — optional. Set to `true` to enable the /bid-tracker
# routes and the Bid Tracker entry in the left nav / mobile menu. Unset/false
# in every build until Bid Tracker is ready to dark-launch or go live per
# environment (same convention as VITE_ADMIN_IMPORT_ENABLED).
#
# VITE_BID_TRACKER_ENABLED=

# VITE_AUTH_PROVIDER — optional. `oauth` signs users in through the GOMS Google OAuth flow (needs VITE_API_BASE_URL and an API with
# AUTH_PROVIDER=both|oauth). Unset or `firebase` keeps today's Firebase Google sign-in (the default; a build without it is unchanged).
#
# VITE_AUTH_PROVIDER=
